cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "CAE Copilot: a validated toolkit for structural CAE and plate vibroacoustics"
abstract: >-
  An open, browser-based toolkit for structural computer-aided engineering and
  the vibroacoustics of thin plates. Generates ready-to-run input decks for
  ABAQUS, ANSYS, LS-DYNA and MATLAB across static, modal, buckling, harmonic,
  explicit-impact and acoustic-radiation analyses, and provides closed-form
  solutions for the same problems so that finite element results can be
  independently cross-checked. Includes functionally graded plate analysis
  referenced to the physical neutral surface, classical lamination theory with
  full ABD assembly and coupling diagnostics, and shear-corrected sandwich
  panel analysis. Natural frequencies are obtained from the exact Levy
  transcendental solution where a simply supported edge pair exists, and from a
  Rayleigh-Ritz formulation using characteristic beam functions otherwise.
  Validated against Leissa (1969) across ten edge-condition cases with a
  maximum error of 0.028 per cent.
